# Banding (CR 702.22): Bot1 attacks with Pikemen (1/1 banding) and Guerrilla Gorilla (2/2) and announces them as a band
# (CR 702.22c, 508.1e). Bot2's Ulvenwald Oddity (4/4) blocks Pikemen, and so blocks the Gorilla too (CR 702.22h: a creature
# blocking a member of a band blocks each other member). The Oddity is blocking a creature with banding, so Bot1, not Bot2,
# divides its 4 damage among the creatures it blocks (CR 702.22k): all of it to Pikemen, which dies, and none to the Gorilla,
# which lives. The band deals 1 + 2 to the Oddity, which lives with 3. Nothing is unblocked: Bot2 stays at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Pikemen
Guerrilla Gorilla
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Ulvenwald Oddity
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pikemen.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ulvenwald Oddity.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Pikemen > Bot2; Guerrilla Gorilla > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Guerrilla Gorilla)
? Combat.Attackers = Pikemen > Bot2 (band 1); Guerrilla Gorilla > Bot2 (band 1)
Bot2.Block(Ulvenwald Oddity > Pikemen)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
? Combat.Blocks = Ulvenwald Oddity > Pikemen; Ulvenwald Oddity > Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.AssignDamage(Ulvenwald Oddity > Pikemen: 4)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Pikemen
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Damage = 3
